         "rnbo_extra_attributes": {
          "code": "// GENERATED by rnbo/tools/build.py from rnbo/src/lxr_engine.cb.js and the\n// firmware sources. Do not edit; edit those and run the script again.\n\n// LXR drum engine for RNBO codebox~\n//\n// A port of the LXR V2 firmware sound engine (Core/Src/Soundengine): three drum voices,\n// snare/clap, cymbal, open/closed hihat, per-voice LFO and velocity modulation, sample\n// rate reduction, the mixer and the FX bus (drive, ring modBuf, compressor, delay).\n//\n// The firmware renders blocks of 64 samples: envelopes, LFOs, modulation and triggers\n// run once per block, the audio paths run per sample in 16-bit integer steps. This port\n// keeps that structure on purpose (same block size, same order of operations, same\n// 16-bit wrap/saturation points, same integer phase accumulators) so it sounds like the\n// hardware and can be checked sample by sample against the original C code\n// (see rnbo/test). Triggers and parameter changes take effect at the next 64-sample\n// block, like on the hardware.\n//\n// Parameters keep the LXR's own value ranges, so an LXR kit's values can be entered\n// 1:1. In the Move patch each one is an RNBO [param] that sets the @param here through\n// [set <name>]. The @param block, scanParams() and the tables are generated by\n// rnbo/tools/build.py from the firmware sources; edit this file, not the generated one.\n//\n// The step sequencer (7 tracks x 16 steps, like the LXR's main steps) runs here too, so\n// its steps land on the same 64-sample blocks as on the hardware. Its pattern is kept\n// in the seq_* parameters, which makes it part of every preset.\n//\n// Inlets  in1:      sequencer control (running + 2 * mute bits);\n//                   [set <param>] messages for the parameters also go here.\n//         in2..in8: triggers for Drum1, Drum2, Drum3, Snare, Cymbal, closed and open hihat.\n//                   Each value is  count * 16384 + note * 128 + velocity ; a new value\n//                   triggers the voice (count only has to change between triggers).\n// Outlets out1/out2: LXR output 1 (stereo), out3/out4: LXR output 2 (stereo).\n//         out5..out22: sequencer state for the Move UI (see seqStatus()).\n\n@param({min: 0, max: 5}) d1_wave = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_coarse = 31;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_fine = 63;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_pwm = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_attack = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_decay = 21;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_slope = 46;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_pitch_decay = 26;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_pitch_slope = 22;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_pitch_amount = 44;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_fm_amount = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_fm_coarse = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 5}) d1_fm_wave = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 1}) d1_fm_mode = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 13}) d1_trans_wave = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_trans_vol = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_trans_freq = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_cutoff = 127;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_reso = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 7}) d1_filter_type = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_filter_drive = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_vel_amount = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 228}) d1_vel_dest = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 1}) d1_vel_volume = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 7}) d1_lfo_wave = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_lfo_rate = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 11}) d1_lfo_sync = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_lfo_amount = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 228}) d1_lfo_dest = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 6}) d1_lfo_retrig = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_lfo_phase = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_volume = 127;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_pan = 63;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_drive = 63;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d1_srate = 127;\n@param({min: 0, max: 6}) d1_out = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 5}) d2_wave = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d2_coarse = 41;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d2_fine = 63;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d2_pwm = 0;\n@param({min: 0, max: 127}) d2_a